# The SHA-256 of wix314-binaries.zip, the portable WiX 3.14 build tools, from
#   https://github.com/wixtoolset/wix3/releases/download/wix314rtm/wix314-binaries.zip
# Get-WiX.ps1 (used by Build-MSI.ps1, release.yml and windows-msi-lab.yml) refuses
# that download unless its SHA-256 equals the first line below that is not a comment:
# 64 hexadecimal digits, nothing else on the line (MA-1103).
#
# This pin is trust on first use. The WiX project publishes no SHA-256 for this zip,
# GitHub records no digest for it (it was uploaded before GitHub kept them), and the
# programs inside are not Authenticode-signed (Get-AuthenticodeSignature: NotSigned on
# candle.exe, light.exe and WixUtilExtension.dll). What it proves: every build uses
# the same bytes as the zip downloaded on the date below.
